Sylvia, I am writing about the Ardsley headquarters at Corbin Tower, which =
your firm designed in 2010 and 2011.<br />
<br />
Over the past year we have had progressive flooring failure across floors 1=
2 through 17. It started as edge lifting in a few areas and it is now wides=
pread, with visible staining, odor complaints and two indoor air quality gr=
ievances from staff. We closed floor 15 in August.<br />
<br />
We retained Kestenbaum Forensic Engineering. Their report is attached. The =
short version is that the resilient flooring assembly was installed directl=
y over the slab with no moisture vapor barrier of any kind, that in-situ re=
lative humidity at depth currently reads 93 to 96%, and that the adhesive h=
as undergone alkaline hydrolysis. Kestenbaum's conclusion is that the assem=
bly was never capable of performing over a lightweight slab in this conditi=
on.<br />
<br />
Our facilities records and our construction file show the finish schedule y=
our firm issued, and it does not include a moisture mitigation system. I wo=
uld like to understand how that happened.
